{"id":"songs-of-innocence-and-of-experience","title":"Songs of Innocence and of Experience","author":"William Blake","year":"1794","note":"Paired lyric cycle — nursery rhyme as political theory.","minutes":120,"cover":"","coverAlt":"","scenes":[{"id":"s0","title":"Chapter 1","place":"Chapter 1","reentry":"SONGS OF INNOCENCE","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s1","title":"Chapter 2","place":"Chapter 2","reentry":"The skylark and thrush,","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s2","title":"Chapter 3","place":"Chapter 3","reentry":"Does thou know who made thee?","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"}],"breaths":[{"id":"s0-0","sceneId":"s0","text":"SONGS OF INNOCENCE"},{"id":"s0-1","sceneId":"s0","text":"INTRODUCTION"},{"id":"s0-2","sceneId":"s0","text":"Piping down the valleys wild,"},{"id":"s0-3","sceneId":"s0","text":"Piping songs of pleasant glee,"},{"id":"s0-4","sceneId":"s0","text":"On a cloud I saw a child,"},{"id":"s0-5","sceneId":"s0","text":"And he laughing said to me:"},{"id":"s0-6","sceneId":"s0","text":"‘Pipe a song about a Lamb!’"},{"id":"s0-7","sceneId":"s0","text":"So I piped with merry cheer."},{"id":"s0-8","sceneId":"s0","text":"‘Piper, pipe that song again.’"},{"id":"s0-9","sceneId":"s0","text":"So I piped: he wept to hear."},{"id":"s0-10","sceneId":"s0","text":"‘Drop thy pipe, thy happy pipe;"},{"id":"s0-11","sceneId":"s0","text":"Sing thy songs of happy cheer!’"},{"id":"s0-12","sceneId":"s0","text":"So I sung the same again,"},{"id":"s0-13","sceneId":"s0","text":"While he wept with joy to hear."},{"id":"s0-14","sceneId":"s0","text":"‘Piper, sit thee down and write"},{"id":"s0-15","sceneId":"s0","text":"In a book, that all may read.’"},{"id":"s0-16","sceneId":"s0","text":"So he vanished from my sight;"},{"id":"s0-17","sceneId":"s0","text":"And I plucked a hollow reed,"},{"id":"s0-18","sceneId":"s0","text":"And I made a rural pen,"},{"id":"s0-19","sceneId":"s0","text":"And I stained the water clear,"},{"id":"s0-20","sceneId":"s0","text":"And I wrote my happy songs"},{"id":"s0-21","sceneId":"s0","text":"Every child may joy to hear."},{"id":"s0-22","sceneId":"s0","text":"THE SHEPHERD"},{"id":"s0-23","sceneId":"s0","text":"How sweet is the shepherd’s sweet lot!"},{"id":"s0-24","sceneId":"s0","text":"From the morn to the evening he strays;"},{"id":"s0-25","sceneId":"s0","text":"He shall follow his sheep all the day,"},{"id":"s0-26","sceneId":"s0","text":"And his tongue shall be fillèd with praise."},{"id":"s0-27","sceneId":"s0","text":"For he hears the lambs’ innocent call,"},{"id":"s0-28","sceneId":"s0","text":"And he hears the ewes’ tender reply;"},{"id":"s0-29","sceneId":"s0","text":"He is watchful while they are in peace,"},{"id":"s0-30","sceneId":"s0","text":"For they know when their shepherd is nigh."},{"id":"s0-31","sceneId":"s0","text":"THE ECHOING GREEN"},{"id":"s0-32","sceneId":"s0","text":"The sun does arise,"},{"id":"s0-33","sceneId":"s0","text":"And make happy the skies;"},{"id":"s0-34","sceneId":"s0","text":"The merry bells ring"},{"id":"s0-35","sceneId":"s0","text":"To welcome the Spring;"},{"id":"s1-0","sceneId":"s1","text":"The skylark and thrush,"},{"id":"s1-1","sceneId":"s1","text":"The birds of the bush,"},{"id":"s1-2","sceneId":"s1","text":"Sing louder around"},{"id":"s1-3","sceneId":"s1","text":"To the bells’ cheerful sound;"},{"id":"s1-4","sceneId":"s1","text":"While our sports shall be seen"},{"id":"s1-5","sceneId":"s1","text":"On the echoing green."},{"id":"s1-6","sceneId":"s1","text":"Old John, with white hair,"},{"id":"s1-7","sceneId":"s1","text":"Does laugh away care,"},{"id":"s1-8","sceneId":"s1","text":"Sitting under the oak,"},{"id":"s1-9","sceneId":"s1","text":"Among the old folk."},{"id":"s1-10","sceneId":"s1","text":"They laugh at our play,"},{"id":"s1-11","sceneId":"s1","text":"And soon they all say,"},{"id":"s1-12","sceneId":"s1","text":"‘Such, such were the joys"},{"id":"s1-13","sceneId":"s1","text":"When we all—girls and boys—"},{"id":"s1-14","sceneId":"s1","text":"In our youth-time were seen"},{"id":"s1-15","sceneId":"s1","text":"On the echoing green.’"},{"id":"s1-16","sceneId":"s1","text":"Till the little ones, weary,"},{"id":"s1-17","sceneId":"s1","text":"No more can be merry:"},{"id":"s1-18","sceneId":"s1","text":"The sun does descend,"},{"id":"s1-19","sceneId":"s1","text":"And our sports have an end."},{"id":"s1-20","sceneId":"s1","text":"Round the laps of their mothers"},{"id":"s1-21","sceneId":"s1","text":"Many sisters and brothers,"},{"id":"s1-22","sceneId":"s1","text":"Like birds in their nest,"},{"id":"s1-23","sceneId":"s1","text":"Are ready for rest,"},{"id":"s1-24","sceneId":"s1","text":"And sport no more seen"},{"id":"s1-25","sceneId":"s1","text":"On the darkening green."},{"id":"s1-26","sceneId":"s1","text":"THE LAMB"},{"id":"s1-27","sceneId":"s1","text":"Little lamb, who made thee?"},{"id":"s1-28","sceneId":"s1","text":"Does thou know who made thee,"},{"id":"s1-29","sceneId":"s1","text":"Gave thee life, and bid thee feed"},{"id":"s1-30","sceneId":"s1","text":"By the stream and o’er the mead;"},{"id":"s1-31","sceneId":"s1","text":"Gave thee clothing of delight,"},{"id":"s1-32","sceneId":"s1","text":"Softest clothing, woolly, bright;"},{"id":"s1-33","sceneId":"s1","text":"Gave thee such a tender voice,"},{"id":"s1-34","sceneId":"s1","text":"Making all the vales rejoice?"},{"id":"s1-35","sceneId":"s1","text":"Little lamb, who made thee?"},{"id":"s2-0","sceneId":"s2","text":"Does thou know who made thee?"},{"id":"s2-1","sceneId":"s2","text":"Little lamb, I’ll tell thee;"},{"id":"s2-2","sceneId":"s2","text":"Little lamb, I’ll tell thee:"},{"id":"s2-3","sceneId":"s2","text":"He is callèd by thy name,"},{"id":"s2-4","sceneId":"s2","text":"For He calls Himself a Lamb."},{"id":"s2-5","sceneId":"s2","text":"He is meek, and He is mild,"},{"id":"s2-6","sceneId":"s2","text":"He became a little child."},{"id":"s2-7","sceneId":"s2","text":"I a child, and thou a lamb,"},{"id":"s2-8","sceneId":"s2","text":"We are callèd by His name."},{"id":"s2-9","sceneId":"s2","text":"Little lamb, God bless thee!"},{"id":"s2-10","sceneId":"s2","text":"Little lamb, God bless thee!"},{"id":"s2-11","sceneId":"s2","text":"THE LITTLE BLACK BOY"},{"id":"s2-12","sceneId":"s2","text":"My mother bore me in the southern wild,"},{"id":"s2-13","sceneId":"s2","text":"And I am black, but O my soul is white!"},{"id":"s2-14","sceneId":"s2","text":"White as an angel is the English child,"},{"id":"s2-15","sceneId":"s2","text":"But I am black, as if bereaved of light."},{"id":"s2-16","sceneId":"s2","text":"My mother taught me underneath a tree,"},{"id":"s2-17","sceneId":"s2","text":"And, sitting down before the heat of day,"},{"id":"s2-18","sceneId":"s2","text":"She took me on her lap and kissèd me,"},{"id":"s2-19","sceneId":"s2","text":"And, pointing to the East, began to say:"},{"id":"s2-20","sceneId":"s2","text":"‘Look on the rising sun: there God does live,"},{"id":"s2-21","sceneId":"s2","text":"And gives His light, and gives His heat away,"},{"id":"s2-22","sceneId":"s2","text":"And flowers and trees and beasts and men receive"},{"id":"s2-23","sceneId":"s2","text":"Comfort in morning, joy in the noonday."}]}